{
  "abstract": "Fix any finite list of parities for the numbers of binary ones in columns 1 through K of a Pascal row. Arbitrarily large rows realize this list in any prescribed arithmetic progression. In particular, each positive integer occurs infinitely often in each progression as the first positive column whose binomial coefficient has even binary digit sum (OEIS A249609). A uniform upper bound on a realizing row gives a lower bound of 1/(4 log(1+sqrt(2))) for the liminf of the record divided by log log X in every positive-modulus progression.",
